From 7c467b1a7064aaff34553711676bbe1f92479320 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 22:24:39 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 09111/11362] Add the scored engine: flag coverage 48 of 95
 becomes 89 of 95

REQ-ARC-BENCH-6269. Closes the gap named when the reachability guard shipped --
47 flags the benchmark could not see, and therefore refused to measure.

The `explore` engine drives `graph_explore_solve_v2`. The other 47 flags are read
by the cascade: induction, the world-model verifier, planning, the frontier tiers.
`--engine scored` drives `E3AgentPolicy` through `arc_leaderboard_eval.run_game`,
which is the same policy `make_carnot_agent(Agent)` builds -- so a flag measured
here is measured on the agent the competition actually runs.

Coverage by engine, computed by transitive import closure rather than asserted:

  explore   48 of 95
  scored    89 of 95
  neither    6

Not a second harness. `lb.run_game` already existed and already returns levels,
actions and efficiency; this reuses it rather than writing a parallel driver that
would drift.

CHARGED ACTIONS, NOT RAW ACTIONS. The live gateway bills resets and the two
differ -- vc33 reports 387 against 400. Reporting the cheaper number would
flatter every efficiency comparison by whatever the reset count happens to be.
Test pinned; flipping it back to `actions` turns that test red.

THE 6 THAT NEITHER ENGINE REACHES are all tooling: a static-validation timeout,
four live-runner execution-binding knobs, a metric-scope guard. `--status` now
prints the module that defines each one, because "6 flags nobody can measure"
reads as a capability gap and a tooling knob is not one. Deliberately NOT
auto-classified by module name -- that is the pattern list that drifts, and it
would let a real capability vanish from the ledger for living in a file with the
wrong name. Print the evidence, let a human classify.

A refusal now routes the reader: a flag refused on `explore` that IS reachable on
`scored` says so. A refusal with no next step is a dead end.

LLM OFF BY DEFAULT, and this is a stated limitation rather than an unconsidered
default. `generate()` returns a failure tuple instead of raising, so a
llama-server that dies mid-sweep degrades the run to LLM-off while still emitting
rows labelled LLM-on -- a clean, error-free row that means nothing.
`scripts/arc_scored_path_lever_harness.py` instruments that properly with
per-cell generator-liveness witnesses. Until this engine carries the same,
`--llm` exists but a flag whose whole effect lives inside induction belongs in
that harness.

Cost measured, not guessed: ~5s per game at budget 400, 20-46s at the shipped
budget of 2000. So `explore` stays the per-milestone heartbeat and `scored` is
the promotion sweep.

29 tests. Three mutations checked: undeclaring the scored entry point turns three
red, and swapping charged_actions for actions turns the billing test red.

